# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RentGH environment variables.
# Copy this file to `.env` (cp .env.example .env) and fill in real values.
# NEVER commit your real `.env` file.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Phase 1: Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL connection string used by Prisma.
# • Zero-install local dev: run `npm run db:local` and use the default below.
# • Your own Postgres:        postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/rentgh
# • Neon / Supabase (cloud):  copy the connection string from their dashboard.
# • Supabase on serverless (Vercel): use the Transaction pooler (port 6543),
#   NOT the Session pooler (5432) — session mode's small client cap is easily
#   exhausted by many lambda instances. Keep `?sslmode=require` on the end;
#   lib/prisma.ts adds pg's libpq-compat flag automatically (Supabase's
#   pooler CA is not in Node's trust store).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:54329/rentgh"

# ── Phase 2: Authentication (NextAuth) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Generate a secret with:  openssl rand -base64 32
# NEXTAUTH_SECRET=""
# The public base URL of the site, e.g. http://localhost:3000
# NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Phase 4: Image uploads (Cloudinary) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Free account: https://cloudinary.com → Console → Settings → API Keys.
# All three stay server-side (browsers only receive short-lived signatures).
# Leave unset to run with photo uploads disabled.
# CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=""
# CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=""
# CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=""

# ── Phase 8: Email notifications ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Resend (https://resend.com) — or swap for Nodemailer SMTP settings in code.
# RESEND_API_KEY=""
# EMAIL_FROM="RentGH <noreply@example.com>"

# ── Dev sandbox only ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No outbound internet? The Next.js image optimizer can't fetch remote
# photos server-side and images look broken. Uncomment so browsers load
# images directly instead. NEVER enable in production.
# NEXT_IMAGE_UNOPTIMIZED="1"
